    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d256">

                <pb facs="0385" n="213" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg213"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111M72/6</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stovall</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berne</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-03-23T10:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 23, 1917, 10 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 6 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>678. Wolff official despatch announces that auxiliary cruiser <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Moewe</hi> has returned to a German port with 592
                    prisoners. These prisoners constitute remainder of crews from ships sunk by <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Moewe</hi>, part of which reached Germany on <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Yarrowdale.</hi>
                </p>
                <p>I suggest that steps be taken immediately through appropriate Spanish diplomatic
                    channels to ascertain if any Americans are among these 592 men and, if so, that
                    permission be granted for them to leave Germany at once. In this connection
                    please see my telegrams regarding treatment in Germany accorded crews from <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Yarrowdale.</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d256-f1"/> All <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Yarrowdale</hi> men testified that alleged quarantine
                    was German pretext for their detention as no contagious diseases had developed
                    among them.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stovall</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
